DETACH PARTITION CONCURRENTLY
=============================

The common shape: a partition descriptor rebuilt while the detach is in
its second phase, usually reached through a cached plan.

  c2fab70248d  2024-06-11  Fix creation of partition descriptor during
                           concurrent detach
      "missing relpartbound for relation %u" when the invalidation lands
      between listing the children and reading relpartbound.
      expect: partitions
      revert: by hand (partdesc.c retry loop).
      status: MISSED.  0 in 6 runs of partitions at the default
              duration, and 0 in 8 across partitions and
              partitioned_pgbench at stressval 4.  (The revert is one
              line: disable the "goto retry" in
              RelationBuildPartitionDesc(), which is all the commit
              added.)
              Why it cannot be reached by load, measured rather than
              argued: a statement that expands a partitioned table takes
              AccessShareLock on every partition and holds it to the end
              of its transaction.  With a session sitting in such a
              transaction, DROP TABLE on one of the partitions waits out
              a 5s lock_timeout on AccessExclusiveLock, and DETACH
              CONCURRENTLY's finalize phase waits for lockers the same
              way.  So the catalog change can never land inside a
              statement that has expanded the table, nor inside a
              transaction that has.  The window is confined to the few
              instructions between plan revalidation and expansion at
              the start of a statement, and no amount of load widens
              that.  This wants an injection point.

